WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.490
A student once told me,

2
00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:03.570
“Nobody knows where I am.”

3
00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:06.160
Then we opened her chat app together.

4
00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:09.370
Her live location had been on for three

5
00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:11.450
days, shared with a whole group.

6
00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:15.370
Today: how your phone knows where you are,

7
00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:17.610
and how you decide who else does.

8
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:21.320
Your phone finds itself in three ways.

9
00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:24.790
Satellites, through GPS, find you

10
00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:26.770
outdoors to within a few metres.

11
00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.720
Nearby Wi-Fi networks help indoors.

12
00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:32.680
And your mobile network always knows

13
00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:35.160
which masts your phone is near, even

14
00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:36.660
with location switched off.

15
00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:39.450
Apps can ask to use that

16
00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:41.790
location, and also your camera,

17
00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:44.550
microphone, contacts and photos.

18
00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:47.960
Each yes you give is called a permission.

19
00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:51.290
Some are needed: a map needs your

20
00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:52.630
location to show the way.

21
00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:53.970
Many are not.

22
00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:56.540
So here's the rule.

23
00:00:57.190 --> 00:01:00.270
Before you tap Allow, ask: does

24
00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:01.910
this app need it to do its job?

25
00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:06.420
If the answer is no, tap Don't allow, and

26
00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:08.200
the app will usually work just fine.

27
00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:11.670
Your phone gives you finer choices too.

28
00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:13.820
Only while using the app,

29
00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:15.260
instead of all the time.

30
00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:17.300
Approximate location,

31
00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:19.260
instead of your exact spot.

32
00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:22.510
And ask every time, for

33
00:01:22.510 --> 00:01:23.810
things you rarely use.

34
00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:25.600
Quick check!

35
00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:28.000
A torch app asks for your

36
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.040
location and your contacts.

37
00:01:30.910 --> 00:01:32.070
What do you allow?

38
00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:33.810
Neither.

39
00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:37.170
A torch needs the light on the back

40
00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:38.650
of your phone, nothing more.

41
00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:41.360
An app that wants far more than it

42
00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:43.680
needs is a reason to delete it.

43
00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:47.170
Live location is useful, because your

44
00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:48.850
family can see you got home safely.

45
00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:52.430
Share it with family or one trusted

46
00:01:52.430 --> 00:01:54.150
friend, never a big group.

47
00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.920
Set a time limit, like one hour.

48
00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:59.700
Then check that it really stopped.

49
00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:03.190
Photos can carry a secret too.

50
00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:06.420
Many phone cameras save where each

51
00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:08.480
photo was taken inside the file,

52
00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:10.540
and some apps pass it on.

53
00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:12.870
Turn off location in your camera

54
00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:15.050
settings, and think twice before

55
00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:16.970
posting your house or your street.

56
00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:18.770
Your turn.

57
00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:21.720
You shared live location with your class

58
00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:24.420
group for a party, and it's still on.

59
00:02:25.070 --> 00:02:26.990
Leave it, or stop it?

60
00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:30.670
Stop it now, because a whole group

61
00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:32.470
shouldn't know where you are all day.

62
00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:35.320
Remember: ask if the app needs it,

63
00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:38.620
choose only while using, share live

64
00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:41.080
location with family for a set time,

65
00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:42.500
and check your photos.

66
00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:46.040
Try it tomorrow: open your phone's

67
00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:48.780
settings, find location, and see

68
00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:49.960
which apps can use it.

69
00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:52.320
Switch it off for any app

70
00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:53.320
that doesn't need it.

71
00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:55.810
If it's a family phone, do it

72
00:02:55.810 --> 00:02:57.450
together with the person who owns it.
